In this course, we will learn CLO fabric in more depth.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:16,000
First, let's get to know the 3D stickers and PBR stickers under the fabric texture attribute.

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:23,000
In 3D software, the physical visual effect of the object is usually expressed by using different PBR stickers.

5
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:27,000
Each sticker represents a visual texture attribute.

6
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:30,000
In CLO, you can use these six stickers.

7
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:37,000
Structure picture,發現 picture, illusion picture, transparent picture, surface roughness and metal picture.

8
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:43,000
When these stickers are used together, the texture will be more complete and realistic.

9
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:45,000
The first one is the structure picture.

10
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Through the structure picture, the color or print of the fabric is displayed in 3D.

11
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:53,000
It is the most important sticker to express the texture visual effect.

12
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:57,000
The發現 picture is the second important sticker that is similar to the structure picture.

13
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:01,000
Through the發現 picture, the fine details of the fabric are displayed.

14
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:03,000
Such as the structure of the edge, the wrinkles, etc.

15
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:07,000
The發現 picture only increases the visual effect of the rough details.

16
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:12,000
From the side, the surface is still smooth and smooth.

17
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:17,000
The illusion picture can show the real roughness of the surface of the fabric.

18
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:20,000
The picture belongs to the gray picture.

19
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:24,000
The closer to the black part, the closer to the bottom of the material.

20
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:27,000
The closer to the white part, the closer to the material.

21
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:29,000
The picture is also the surface of the material.

22
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:33,000
In some cases, the illusion picture will add a high-definition blur.

23
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:35,000
To make the edges of the smooth figure.

24
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:43,000
The transparent picture defines the transparent and translucent degree of the surface of the fabric in some areas.

25
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:51,000
In CLO, there are two different sticker modes that express the transparency of the material, RGB and Alpha.

26
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:54,000
The RGB mode uses a gray picture with no transparency.

27
00:01:54,000 --> 00:02:04,000
The closer the JPEG or JPEG to the white area, the less transparent it is, and the closer it is to the black area, the more transparent it is.

28
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:07,000
The depth of the grayness determines the degree of transparency.

29
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:13,000
In the alpha mode, use pictures in the form of .png, .tif, or .psd.

30
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:20,000
The alpha value of the transparent channel reflects the transparency effect.

31
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:28,000
The surface rough map controls the light information on the surface of the fabric, and thus expresses the roughness of the surface of the fabric.

32
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:30,000
The sticker is a gray map.

33
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:33,000
The closer to black, the more reflected light.

34
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:37,000
The closer to white, the less reflected light.

35
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:42,000
The metal map defines the area of the surface of the fabric with metal characteristics.

36
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:44,000
The sticker is a black and white image.

37
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:47,000
The black area represents non-metal materials.

38
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:50,000
The white area represents metal materials.

39
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:55,000
In CLO, the user can set the surface roughness plus the metalness,

40
00:02:55,000 --> 00:03:00,000
and then combine the metal map to express the metal effect of the surface of the fabric.

41
